# AI Playbook Reference

This repository is the AI Playbook itself (a reference guide app plus a portable example package at `ai-playbook/`). Migrated from the legacy single `.cursorrules` file — Cursor's Agent mode ignores that format, so this `.mdc` rule replaces it.

## Working on this repo's own app (`src/`)

This is a React 19 + TypeScript + Vite app using Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui. See [docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md](../../docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md) for the full stack. No playbook lookup needed for UI work.

## Working on the example package (`ai-playbook/`)

Canonical source for every agent/skill is `ai-playbook/.claude/skills/` and `ai-playbook/.claude/agents/` — edit there first, then port changes to `ai-playbook/.github/`, `ai-playbook/.cursor/`, and `ai-playbook/AGENTS.md` + `ai-playbook/.agents/skills/` using the mapping in `ai-playbook/.claude/skills/ai-tool-setup/references/skill-routing.md`.

Detect project type: `node ai-playbook/tools/project-detect.mjs <targetFolder>`

## Scope Enforcement

- Only modify files within the stated target project folder.
- Run `node ai-playbook/tools/scope-guard.mjs <targetFolder> <changedFiles...>` before finalizing changes to the example package.

## Code Style

- Minimal diffs: change only the lines necessary.
- Do not reformat unrelated code or reorganize imports.
- Use forward slashes in all file paths.

## Security

- Never hardcode secrets, API keys, or passwords.
- Validate and sanitize all user inputs.

## Testing

- Run `npm test` to execute the test suite.
- Run `npm run lint` for linting.
- Run `npx tsc --noEmit` for type checking.
